  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice. \r\rS04\rS05 Rev. A\rCA01\rPD03 Rev.J\rPD01 Rev.G\rPD04 Rev.I\rPD06\rFlood Response Management Plan (HDC/1074/03 REV D)\rFlood Risk Assessment Report (HDC/1074/11 REV C)\rHeritage Statement\rPlanning Statement\rS01\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To ensure a design which complies with Development Plan Policies.\r",
    "Prior to occupation of the development, a Verification Report demonstrating that the approved Flood Risk measures have been fully implemented shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority for approval in writing. This report must include:\r\ro\tAs built drawings of the sustainable drainage systems including level information (if appropriate)\ro\tPhotographs of the completed sustainable drainage systems\ro\tAny relevant certificates from manufacturers/ suppliers of any drainage features\ro\tA confirmation statement of the above signed by the site manager or similar\r\rREASON : To ensure the sustainable management of water, minimise flood risk, minimise discharge of surface water outside of the curtilage of the property and ensure that the drainage system will remain functional throughout the lifetime of the development in accordance with Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy, DMD 61, and Policies SI12 & SI13 of the London Plan and the NPPF.\r",
    "The new window and door on the side elevations hereby approved shall be obscurely glazed and non-opening unless parts of the window which can be opened are more than 1.7 metres above the floor of the room in which the window is installed.\rThe glazing shall not be altered without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority.\rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining and neighbouring properties.\r"
  ],
